<title>TAIWAN: TAIWAN CPC JULY PROFIT UP ON FALLING CRUDE COSTS.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN CPC JULY PROFIT UP ON FALLING CRUDE COSTS.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp said on Friday its July pre-tax profit was T$2.435 billion, up from June's pre-tax profit of T$1.864 billion.</p>
<p>&quot;Chinese Petroleum posted July pre-tax profit mainly due to falling crude import costs during the period,&quot; a company official said.</p>
<p>Chinese Petroleum's July crude oil imports cost averaged $17.44 a barrel, lower than its budgeted costs of $17.50 and a hefty $1.22 lower than its June purchases, officials said.</p>
